   "source": [
    "### Parsing the timestamp\n",
    "\n",
    "The format in the file is day-month-year, e.g. `01-01-2018 00:15`. We give pandas the exact format\n",
    "(`%d-%m-%Y %H:%M`) instead of letting it guess, because guessing could mix up day and month\n",
    "(e.g. `01-02-2018` could be read as 2 January or 1 February)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 429,
   "id": "1f7c0a47",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-07T07:45:52.974128Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-07T07:45:52.974067Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-07T07:45:53.014084Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-07T07:45:53.013685Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "2018-01-01 00:15:00\n",
      "2018-01-01 00:30:00\n",
      "2018-01-01 00:45:00\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "df[\"date_time\"] = pd.to_datetime(df[\"date_time\"], format=\"%d-%m-%Y %H:%M\")\n",
    "df[\"date_time\"].head(3)"
   ]
  }
